skill: "affiliate-program-ops"
sections[3]:
  - "# affiliate-program-ops\n\nOperate the affiliate program end to end: commission tiers, fraud rules, monthly payout reconciliation and a quarterly channel audit. Use when affiliates are onboarded, when payout reports arrive from the network, or when acquisition cost per channel is due for review before budget moves.\n\nOwner: role-partnership-bd-manager (pod-growth, marketing). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[5]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - search_web\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"program policy affiliate-policy.toon (tiers, cookie window, exclusions); network payout report for the period; billing ledger export from billing-automation; acquisition spend by channel channel-spend.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/growth/affiliate-register.toon; payout-recon.toon with matched and break entries; channel-audit.toon with effective CAC per channel\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load affiliate-policy.toon; confirm tier thresholds and the cookie window are unchanged for this period, otherwise note the policy version in the report.\n2. Apply the fraud rules to the network report before any payout math: self-referrals, incentivized traffic patterns, conversion clusters outside plausible hours and duplicate devices.\n3. Hold flagged conversions out of the payable set; record the rule that fired per flag so the decision is reproducible.\n4. Reconcile the payable set against the billing ledger: matched conversions, missing attribution entries and ledger conversions with no network record.\n5. Compute the payout total per affiliate per tier with run_command; round according to the policy and never by hand.\n6. Draft the payout file for approval; emit ask_question to the operator for any payout above the single-payment approval threshold.\n7. On approval, hand the payout instruction to role-accounts-manager; affiliate payouts go through the same ledger discipline as any other payable.\n8. Compute effective CAC per channel for the quarter and write channel-audit.toon; flag any channel whose CAC crosses the budget ceiling two quarters running.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\npayout instructions to role-accounts-manager; CAC audit feeds growth budget review.\n"
